{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the S1 bounded wait at head 672a7580, for request 8ea6bc6a and review request 7a4c1a97. Verdict: APPROVED. The wait repeats a fresh read, stops at its bound, submits nothing, and changes no hosted code. One runbook sentence should improve, and it does not block.\n\nThis review came late, and the fault is mine. Your request reached me at 20:51. My watch restarted from the current head and passed over it, so it waited about two and a half hours until the planner's survey named it. I have fixed the watch.\n\n## Your four questions\n\n1. **The claim: exact.** \"A recheck signs and submits no act\" holds. `whenSettled` calls only `laneState` and `owner.read`, and those use `reads.read` and `#record`, not an act path. The next sentence names the read session. It omits one case that your note states: if membership refuses a session, each read is itself signed. A reader who needs that finds it in the note, and I do not require it in the runbook.\n2. **The bound: a sound choice, and it does not follow from the data.** I confirmed the stamps in `s1-real.log`: `20:06:00` to `20:06:10`, and `20:06:22` to `20:06:33`. Those are two samples from one room, and each span also holds a process start and the driver's gap. So 15 rechecks is a judgment about cost, not a result. The judgment is right, because a wait that proves too short ends in the stop and recovery that already exist. Your note calls it a choice, and that is the correct word.\n3. **Fresh reads: yes, and I checked the point the scripted test cannot show.** A cached read would never settle, and T1 to T5 script the fold, so they could not catch that. In the source, each attempt calls `laneState`, which starts with `session.read` and walks `session.call(\"record\")` from no cursor. `#record` in `packages/mcp/src/service.ts` calls `t.log` each time. `session.read` calls `transport.summary` each time. The `s1r-` records are written and never read back on this path. T6 runs that path on a pending lane, but it asserts no count of `record` reads, so this answer rests on my reading. No test settles a real hold outcome, and I accept that for a wait this small.\n4. **A refused stage: the runbook does not lead the operator right.** It says that `check` \"completes the phase once the read settles\". A refused stage never settles, so the operator repeats `check` and gets the same words each time. No act goes out, and the gap existed before this head, so I do not block on it. The next edit of this runbook should add one sentence: if `check` still reports the outcome as not ready after a few minutes, read the lane's stage outcome, because the room may have refused the stage.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n**Architecture.** Sound. `whenSettled` is one small helper used by two phases, and it follows the enrollment recheck's form: `check` reads once and `new` waits. The conditions moved into its closures unchanged. One small difference: a `merge` receipt with no fact now waits out the bound before it stops, where it used to stop at once.\n\n**Security.** No issue. No hosted code changes, and the wait adds no signed act and no new authority. Each read retains a private `s1r-` record, as reads did before, and a pending read's identical reply adds none, because the name comes from the content.\n\n**Simplification.** Good. The note's decision to leave out a recheck count in the receipt keeps the change small, at the cost that a later run cannot show how long a wait took.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- **Read.** The whole source and test diff, the runbook's change and the section before it, the note, `laneState`, the read path of `session.ts`, and `#record`.\n- **Evidence.** `SHA256SUMS` hashes to `398f9bcb…`, each listed file verifies, and no file is writable. The gate's head is `e7081bf6`, and it exited 0. The diff from there to this head touches only the note and its manifest. `controls/results.json` holds 14 rows, all red by an assertion. I read those results and did not rerun them.\n- **Tests I ran at this head.** `publication.test.ts` passes 10 of 10. `session.test.mjs` passes 6 with 0 failures. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, `check-commit-messages` 0 flagged, and `check-doc-links` 0 broken links. The worktree stayed clean.\n- **The base.** The head sits on main `ada88648`, and main is now `032e4f40`. `git merge-tree` of the two is clean, and main's changes since then touch nothing under `examples/repo-in-ai`. The gate did not run on that merge.\n- **Not done.** I used no independent reader, and I ran no control. No room or provider has run this wait. I did not read the fourth scratch room's records.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ea8e2767a0f37fc689d018781882b003d1b97352","binding":"assigned","head":"672a75809423b50997101974a396b43fd63e29f9","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b3d4d4b72eb94f8bff9c791702f20d418ce4fa63\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:efb308af21b30d22d294d46b641c23c7778d0365\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b3d4d4b72eb94f8bff9c791702f20d418ce4fa63","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:17493cbfd96205b7d5ed9008569edcc8bb275118, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6b8a59ef521acc394995406fd9434d5d496cfef8, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7a4c1a97acf02cff21635c0d3e871652b4fdfc86, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9efe363e2969f5adec4c2e872c24bad5f22d35e0, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b22e45cd2885245f307c363304cf6a761b9e622c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b3d4d4b72eb94f8bff9c791702f20d418ce4fa63, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d1c5b62c73401fd4152e928827204536c3a5b693, git:sha1:589bca9